              "role": "user",
              "content": "=Create a Twitter/X thread from this article.\n\nArticle Title: {{ $json.article.title }}\nArticle Content: {{ $json.article.body }}\nAuthor Handle: {{ $json.author_handle }}\n\nRules:\n- Create exactly 5-7 tweets in a thread\n- Tweet 1: Strong hook that creates curiosity (no \"Thread:\" or \"1/\" prefix). Use a pattern interrupt.\n- Tweets 2-5: Key insights, one per tweet. Use concrete examples, data, or analogies.\n- Tweet 6: Practical takeaway or actionable advice\n- Final tweet: CTA to read the full article + \"Follow {{ $json.author_handle }} for more\"\n- Each tweet MUST be under 280 characters (this is critical)\n- Use line breaks within tweets for readability\n- Include 1-2 relevant emojis per tweet maximum\n- No hashtags except in the final tweet (max 2)\n- Number format: use \"1/\" at the start of each tweet\n\nReturn the thread as a JSON array of strings, one string per tweet. Example:\n[\"1/ Hook tweet here\", \"2/ Second tweet here\", \"3/ Third tweet here\"]\n\nReturn ONLY the JSON array, no other text."
